From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: Shell.Application's folders, items, shortcuts and verbs work

Most of Shell.Application's object model returned E_NOTIMPL: scripts
(VBScript, JScript, PowerShell through COM) and installers could not copy
or move with Folder.CopyHere/MoveHere -- the usual way a script copies
into a folder --, make a folder, walk Items() or Verbs() with For Each,
read an item's size, type or date, rename it, run a verb on it, or read
and change a shortcut through FolderItem.GetLink.

- Folder: CopyHere and MoveHere (a path, a FolderItem or FolderItems;
  the options are FOF_ flags; done with SHFileOperation before returning),
  NewFolder, ParentFolder, GetDetailsOf (an item's column text, or with no
  item the column's name), OfflineStatus (offline files are not in use),
  Synchronize, and the web view barricade properties (none).
- FolderItem: Name can be set (renamed through the folder), GetFolder,
  ModifyDate (read and set, local time), Size, Type (as Explorer names
  it), InvokeVerb/InvokeVerbEx (a canonical verb or a menu entry's text;
  none: the default), ExtendedProperty (canonical names or "{fmtid} pid",
  the folder's details first, then the file system's).
- FolderItems: _NewEnum, any numeric index, InvokeVerbEx on all the items
  at once, Filter (SHCONTF_ flags and wildcards), Verbs (those the items
  share).
- FolderItemVerbs: _NewEnum; FolderItemVerb: DoIt.
- ShellLinkObject: every property can be read and set (path, description,
  working directory, arguments, hotkey, show command, icon), Resolve,
  Save (to its file or another), Target.
- The item context menu takes any verb of the file type by name ("open",
  "edit", "print", "runas"), listed or not, as Windows' does; such a verb
  was "Unhandled string verb".

Wine's shell32 shelldispatch tests: eleven todo_wine pass and are removed;
shlfolder and shelllink tests: no change.

Gate: test/shellapp-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit cscript, test/shellapp.js).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_COPYHERE (shell32/shelldispatch.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_REGISTRY_VERBS (shell32/shlview_cmenu.c).
